### Description

Refactor app to open directly in Notes list without any startup authentication. Remove the Relux Sample landing screen and dead main/auth/logout entry routes. Move Account into a native Settings destination accessible from Notes toolbar. Repurpose existing Auth package as reusable system device-owner authentication for individual notes, not app-global login. Add per-note lock/unlock and explicit relock/remove-lock controls with simple native UI. Preserve iOS17/macOS14, glass availability fallbacks, KISS/DRY/SOLID and Relux dispatch-in-container, service/provider boundaries. Before behavioral refactors add focused Swift Testing coverage. No CUA, screenshots, simulator navigation, snapshot harnesses or UI tests: user explicitly requested blind best effort. Existing in-memory storage stays in-memory. Parent owns signed PR publication; leave candidate uncommitted for board handoff. Write a concise .spec/note-protection.md before implementation.
### Acceptance Criteria

Launch immediately shows Notes without system auth; Settings contains Account; old landing screen is removed. Locked note bodies are hidden from list/search/details/editor until that specific note is successfully authenticated using biometry or device credential fallback. Failed/false/cancelled/unavailable auth never grants access. Lock state survives refresh/edit in the in-memory provider; access is revoked on manual relock and app background, and late auth cannot regrant revoked access. Focused unit tests and iOS build pass; no deep UI testing

## Instructions

The following instructions have been attached to this task:

### protection-decisions.md
> Settled behavior and scope boundaries

Titles remain visible for identifying notes; locked bodies must not appear in row previews, body search, details or editing props. Auth success authorizes only the requested note, not every note. Protect destructive/edit/remove-protection paths consistently; guard in domain/provider as appropriate, not only by hiding buttons. Keep protection metadata in the in-memory provider so reload/upsert cannot silently remove it; transient unlock grants are not persisted. Relock on explicit action and when app enters background (NOT inactive, which may occur during the system auth prompt). A result arriving after background/relock must not grant access: use a minimal operation/session generation check or equally simple correct approach. Prefer fresh LAContext per evaluation to avoid unintended credential reuse. System .deviceOwnerAuthentication supplies biometry or device passcode/macOS password fallback; failure/unavailability fails closed, no custom password or mock bypass. Remove app-global login/logout screens and routes that are now dead. Auth remains useful domain example behind interfaces; Notes must not import AuthServiceImpl or LocalAuthentication. Prefer result-bearing Flow for reusable authentication and straightforward coordination; inspect upstream API and choose least coupling. No at-rest encryption/persistence/network scope: docs describe an in-memory sample access lock honestly. Keep ordinary notes immediately editable without any auth. Prior user explicitly forbids expensive UI testing: no CUA/screenshot/snapshot/device-navigation work. Source is clean current main 7480dda. Parent owns publication, not worker.




